    "title": "Pass happy: Play Football First Play gets Hall of Fame Week activities rolling in Canton - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CANTON ‒ Nearly 2,500 children formed a line to pass a football from downtown Canton to the Pro Football Hall of Fame on the morning of July 30 for the 25th annual Play Football First Play event. The three-mile route started at the Frank T. Bow building, the location in downtown Canton where the NFL was founded when it was the site of Ralph Hay’s Hupmobile car showroom. Among the participants were best friends Major Williams, 9, and Gio Gardner, 10, both of Canton. Both play football on their respective youth teams. Major is a quarterback, and Gio, a wide receiver. They had similar reasons for attending First Play. \"I'm a big football fan and I love the Chiefs ,\" said Major. \"I like football. I love the Vikings,\" said Gio. Elise Lockwood, 8, of Canton, was participating in her sixth First Play, accompanied by her 4-year-old brother Wyatt. She said she attended the event to pass the football, although her personal physical pursuits are dance and cheerleading. In addition to going for the long yardage, participants were able to visit the new First Play Festival, featuring inflatables, football stations and gaming trucks at the hall. Four Hall of Famers walked the route: Joe DeLamielleure, Elvin Bethea, Robert Brazile and Bryant Young. This article originally appeared on The Repository: Pass happy: Play Football First Play gets Hall of Fame Week activities rolling in Canton",
